      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "if your PC can't even run a 64-bit version of Windows, then playing VRChat is out of the question, hate to break it to you.\n\nThe newest 32-bit only CPU that uses the x86 arch was the Pentium 4 from Intel...and 32 bit operating systems can only use an absolute maximum of 4GB of RAM (usually closer to 3.5GB), and VRChat usually eats up 2-3 GB of RAM on larger worlds for me, so playing VRChat on a 32 bit CPU, or at least a 32 bit OS is out of the question",
